        "original_id": "6c421cf6-b3c8-5f16-9c57-e893e02ccec8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Peter Desaga, Michael Faraday, Robert Wilhelm Bunsen\n- Organizations: University of Heidelberg\n- Products: Bunsen burner, laboratory burner\n- Concepts: electromagnetism, electrochemistry\n\nFacts:\n- Michael Faraday was an English scientist who lived from 22 September 1791 to 25 August 1867.\n- Michael Faraday contributed to the study of electromagnetism and electrochemistry.\n- Peter Desaga was a German instrument maker at the University of Heidelberg who worked with Robert Wilhelm Bunsen.\n- In 1855, Peter Desaga perfected an earlier laboratory burner design by Michael Faraday into the Bunsen burner.\n- Robert Wilhelm Bunsen and his laboratory assistant Peter Desaga developed the Bunsen burner as an improvement on earlier laboratory burners.",
